    "Scouting Notes": "POST DRAFT NOTES\n Makes some of the best swing decisions in the class\n Raw power isn't insane, Max EV's aren't crazy, but he has the potential for 25-30 HR power because he elevates to the pull side a ton\n Hit tool has a chance to be solid as well\n Possibility for one of the more well rounded offensive profiles in the draft\n Not a bad athlete, but not a great one either, likely a 40 grade runner as he ages and adds some more weight\n Defense at third was not good at previous stops, first base should be average or better defensively\n Arm is good enough to handle other spots, maybe could handle a corner OF spot?\n The bat is what you're buying and maybe the Brewers can help him figure out third to enough of a degree where he can at least hold it down\n Michael Busch is a pretty fun comp if he doesn't stick at third, but could be better if he can stick there",
